<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Shelon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1471">1471</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Battle of the Shelon River, Battle of the Shelon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shelon-river">Shelon</a> was fought on 14 July 1471 on the Shelon river, west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-ilmen">Lake Ilmen</a>, between the army of the Novgorod Republic and the forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iii">Ivan III</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>. The much larger but poorly led Novgorod militia was routed. The defeat forced Novgorod to accept the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-korostyn">Treaty of Korostyn</a>, renouncing ties with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>, and opened the way to its annexation by Moscow in 1478.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-shelon.jpg" alt="Battle of Shelon" width="320" height="438" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous Russian manuscript illuminators, 1560-1570s Facial Chronicle (Illustrated Chronicle of Ivan the Terrible) (... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Facial_Chronicle_-_b.15,_p._243.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
